# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
# Sequence generation scratch files
task/sequences/sweep/
task/sequences/diagnostics/
task/sequences/all_sequences.pkl
/tmp/seq_pool/
/tmp/seq_pool_cont/
/tmp/test_prefix3/
/tmp/test_prefix3_runs/
scripts/sweep_sequences.py
scripts/test_sequences_subsampling.py
task/sequences/sequences.json
task/sequences/sequences.pkl

# Per-participant sequence pool (task/generate_sequences_pool.py output) --
# 800 small files (200 members x 2 tasks x .pkl/.json) is too much file-count
# churn for git to track usefully, and it's fully reproducible on demand via
# `python task/generate_sequences_pool.py --n_pool 200 --task both --seed 0`
# (the exact promoted parameters live in that script's own CLI defaults) --
# resolves the earlier open question about whether to commit this pool or
# consolidate it into fewer files: neither, just don't track it at all.
task/sequences_pool/

# Backup of the deterministic-prefix binary pool, taken before switching
# production to the no-prefix scheme (chat history) -- same reasoning as
# task/sequences_pool/ above (large per-participant file count, and this
# is specifically the OLD scheme, fully reproducible on demand via
# `python task/generate_sequences_pool.py --n_pool 200 --task binary --seed 0`
# with the prefix-based defaults, i.e. without --no_prefix), not something
# that needs to live in git history to be recoverable.
task/sequences_pool_binary_prefix_backup/

# Canonical production datasets, built by scripts/pull_soltani_data.py
# (complete_pairs + the non_integrator exclusion criterion). TRACKED (not
# gitignored, per instruction) -- unlike an earlier version of this file,
# which gitignored them; that was the inconsistent choice, since
# carrabin.pkl/yoo.pkl (the un-ignore overrides above) are already tracked
# the same way. Github is now the sync channel between this machine and the
# cluster for these two files specifically -- rebuild with:
#   venv/bin/python scripts/pull_soltani_data.py --complete_pairs

# Private prolific_pid -> anonymized-pid registry (utils/pid_registry.py).
# Contains REAL Prolific participant IDs, unlike soltani_numbers.pkl/
# soltani_colors.pkl just above (or any canonical data/*.pkl), which only
# ever get the anonymized integer -- must NEVER be tracked, and specifically
# must NEVER go through GitHub even though the two files above now do.
# Already covered by the wholesale data/ ignore at the top of this section
# (no !-override exists for it), but called out explicitly here too, since
# its sensitivity is categorically higher than the rest of data/. If a build
# needs to run somewhere else (e.g. the cluster), copy this one file there
# directly (scp/rsync, never git) so both places assign the same integer
# pid to the same real person.
data/pid_registry.json

# Vite build output and npm dependencies
task/node_modules/
task/dist-continuous/
task/dist-binary/
task/dist/
task/jatos.js
